Z||000000||Ed||03-05-2000||05:38 PM||||I read here before about monofilament being used to attach the clear sail panel on the GT's. <P>Monofilament has worked it's way out from the bottom of the (original) plastic sail panel of my '87 GT. Does this mean anything? Or can I just cut off the offending line?   ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||03-05-2000||05:59 PM||||Just lop it off. Its purpose was to aid in the removal of the 1/4 window. You pull it and it is supposed to cut through the double faced tape that holds the window on.||||reg||1
